Now let me understand the task. Ticket 03: make the two endings visibly different.

Requirements:
1. Line win highlights exactly the three cells of the winning Line reported by the engine.
2. When no Line is reported, no cell is highlighted.
3. Fill win presents the full Board with no Line highlighted, visually distinct from a Line win.
4. Line win on ninth move highlights the Line rather than presented as Fill win.
5. Highlight and distinct-Fill treatment driven only by engine's status; UI holds no rule logic.
6. Starting a new game clears any highlight and ending treatment.

The engine already reports `reason`, `line`, `winner`. The UI currently renders board and status. The engine tests presumably already cover the ninth-move line precedence. We need UI changes. Since the UI is logic-free, the change is only in ui.js and styles.css. No engine change needed.

TDD: The AGENTS says no test runner. The spec says no automated tests. "Use /tdd where possible, at pre-agreed seams." The engine seam is already implemented; the change here is pure presentation. There is no test runner and it's explicitly out of scope. So TDD isn't really possible/applicable here. I should verify manually via browser.

Let me check the docs/agents/triage-labels to update status? The issue status is ready-for-agent. Previous commits didn't update statuses? Let me check whether ticket files were modified after implementation (git log for scratch files). Actually commit 2fe2397 "docs: break down spec into tickets" added them all. Then feats didn't touch them. So no status updates. Fine.

Let me think about the UI design for the highlight and fill treatment.

Current render:
```js
